arentName":"Novéant-sur-Moselle","dept":"57","lon":6.03177,"lat":49.04113,"tier":"regional","subregion":"lorraine","slug":"noveant-sur-moselle","id":"al_village_57515","vineyardHa":2.9,"aoc":1,"lieuxDits":5,"bounds":[6.03912,49.01523,6.04323,49.01738],"placedHa":2.9},"al_village_57642":{"nom":"Scy-Chazelles","code":"57642","parent":"57642","parentName":"Scy-Chazelles","dept":"57","lon":6.12112,"lat":49.11455,"tier":"regional","subregion":"lorraine","slug":"scy-chazelles","id":"al_village_57642","vineyardHa":4.3,"aoc":1,"lieuxDits":4,"bounds":[6.10761,49.11567,6.12771,49.12015],"placedHa":4.3},"al_village_57650":{"nom":"Sierck-les-Bains","code":"57650","parent":"57650","parentName":"Sierck-les-Bains","dept":"57","lon":6.35976,"lat":49.43633,"tier":"regional","subregion":"lorraine","slug":"sierck-les-bains","id":"al_village_57650","vineyardHa":31.8,"aoc":1,"lieuxDits":7,"bounds":[6.35521,49.44479,6.37021,49.4594],"placedHa":31.7},"al_village_57701":{"nom":"Vaux","code":"57701","parent":"57701","parentName":"Vaux","dept":"57","lon":6.06593,"lat":49.09267,"tier":"regional","subregion":"lorraine","slug":"vaux","id":"al_village_57701","vineyardHa":3.4,"aoc":1,"lieuxDits":5,"bounds":[6.07707,49.09435,6.08413,49.09633],"placedHa":3.4},"al_village_57712":{"nom":"Vic-sur-Seille","code":"57712","parent":"57712","parentName":"Vic-sur-Seille","dept":"57","lon":6.52632,"lat":48.77513,"tier":"regional","subregion":"lorraine","slug":"vic-sur-seille","id":"al_village_57712","vineyardHa":9,"aoc":1,"lieuxDits":6,"bounds":[6.51258,48.78656,6.54664,48.79114],"placedHa":9}},"sources":[{"name":"INAO — Délimitation des aires géographiques des SIQO","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/5d7fb2856f444171a5f2780b"},{"name":"INAO — Délimitation parcellaire des AOC viticoles","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/5aaf6b7ec751df67b0d7a87f"},{"name":"geo.api.gouv.fr — communes (IGN Admin Express)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://geo.api.gouv.fr"},{"name":"IGN — BD TOPO®, vine zones (zone de végétation « Vigne »)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://geoservices.ign.fr/bdtopo"},{"name":"Cadastre Etalab — lieux-dits","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://cadastre.data.gouv.fr"},{"name":"BRGM — Cartes géologiques harmonisées à 1/50 000 (BD Charm-50)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://infoterre.brgm.fr"},{"name":"INRAE — Carte des sols de France (soil types, via IGN Géoplateforme)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://www.gissol.fr"},{"name":"Météo-France — SIM quotidienne (Safran-Isba reanalysis, 8 km grid)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/donnees-changement-climatique-sim-quotidienne"}],"truthBoundary":["The levels come from the structure of the INAO appellations: an Alsace grand cru is its own appellation (51 named sites), a named area is a “dénomination géographique complémentaire” (Alsace + place name), everything else is regional.","Lorraine (Moselle and Côtes de Toul, in INAO’s Colmar office) is grouped here with Alsace for convenience; it is a separate, much smaller vineyard.","Vineyard land is the vine cover mapped by IGN in BD TOPO, not the INAO parcel delimitation.","Appellation areas come from the INAO parcel delimitation (informational; the official plan is the one filed at the town hall or with INAO) cut to the mapped vines. Where an appellation shape and a lieu-dit are too complex for an exact intersection, their overlap is measured on a grid of points (typically within about one point of the place’s area).","Surface geology is the rock unit mapped at 1:50 000 under the plot, not the soil. Where the legend states no stage, age is inferred from the unit’s name, code or kind (marked ≈) or left blank.","Weather is the Météo-France SIM reanalysis (Safran-Isba, built from ground observations) for the surrounding 8 km grid cell, not a measurement on the plot. Its daily extremes come from hourly values: against 16 Météo-France stations it ran typically 0.5–2 °C below measured maximum temperatures, differed on minimum temperatures by up to about 2 °C either way, and missed hot days and local cold-air pockets. Daily rain and temperatures tracked the stations closely. GDD base 10 °C, evapotranspiration is Météo-France potential evapotranspiration, climate type from 1991–2020 monthly normals.","Soil type is the dominant type mapped by INRAE at regional scale where the plot lies, not a measurement on the plot."]}